Fix several Wayland server bugs on Ubuntu 26.04 GNOME: (1) moving the cursor
to a screen corner with no adjacent client could permanently freeze the cursor
because InputCapture barriers were installed on all four edges by default —
barriers are now installed only for sides reported active by the server via
reconfigure(); (2) a safety watchdog releases any stuck InputCapture after
1 second when there is no adjacent screen (hot-corner), but no longer fires
during normal secondary-screen control so it cannot interrupt ongoing input
forwarding; (3) the InputCapture session is kept active throughout secondary
control — the physical cursor stays at the barrier and all EI motion and button
events continue flowing to InputLeap, eliminating cursor oscillation and clicks
incorrectly returning to the primary screen; (4) cursor position on the primary
screen is tracked correctly by accumulating EI relative-motion events.
